11374	{"artifactId":"LLD-0f17539c98aa78ee-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-0f17539c98aa78ee-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:08:09.918Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The route the ISSUE says cannot work really cannot, and the shared enumeration can be consumed unchanged as the replacement (subject = topic, repoPath, db, maxSources, runId, no area, a stand-in provider for tests), with its completeness foldable into the check's.","evidence":"validate.ts:438-442 isTargetCompatible returns true only for the same target or a 'generic' plan, so a code/data/infra plan cannot hold docs.constraint.enumerate. doc-constraint-enumerate.ts:97-109 RunDocConstraintEnumerateArgs has subject, repoPath, db, area?, maxSources?, runId?, logContext?, provider?; with no area retrieval runs over closureRepos [repoPath] (lines 212-221). It throws LookupFailedError on a failed model call (150-154) and returns constraints [] with retrievedSectionCount 0 on no match (228-238). Its output carries limited/skipped/partlyRead through carriedCompleteness, and graphCompleteness (completeness-facts.ts:66-74) already accepts `skipped`, so the fold the design describes is possible. The three fix-intent bullets (refuse at validation, a working route, descriptions naming only working routes) are each covered; the misread constraintsSource is removed rather than repaired, which the stakeholder decision cited in the design allows. [files: src/analyze/planner/validate.ts, src/analyze/explore/doc-constraint-enumerate.ts, src/analyze/explore/completeness-facts.ts]","action":"None. Note for the build: maxSources is clamped to 1..30 and defaults to 15 inside the enumeration, so a task giving 15 and a task giving nothing get two records under the proposed key; harmless, but say so in the record module's comment.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today resolveConstraints reads constraintsSource from upstreamOutputs first, then takes ANY array as the inline list, then non-empty constraintIds, and returns [] otherwise, on which runAdherenceCheck throws 'no constraints available'.","evidence":"adherence.ts:349-358 reads params['constraintsSource'] and args.upstreamOutputs.get(source), falling through when the upstream is absent; 361-364 `if (Array.isArray(inline)) return normaliseConstraints(inline);` (so an empty inline list beside usable ids returns [] — the design's stated behaviour change is real); 371-377 ids only when length > 0; 379 `return [];`; 211-218 throws `${templateId}: no constraints available. Provide one of: params.constraintsSource ...`. executor/types.ts:43 says upstreamOutputs is keyed by produces-name, as the design says. [files: src/analyze/runtimes/shared/adherence.ts, src/analyze/executor/types.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The three adherence templates require only their subject, declare constraintsSource/constraints/constraintIds as optional, are at revision 'r1', and their descriptions point the planner at the upstream docs task.","evidence":"infra/index.ts:152-182: revision 'r1', `required: ['infraSubject']`, `additionalProperties: false`, `constraintsSource: { type: 'string' }`, description 'constraints come from an upstream docs.constraint.enumerate task OR params.constraints inline'. code/index.ts:186-231: same shape, with the descriptions the design quotes ('used when the plan does not have an upstream docs.constraint.enumerate task', 'used when constraintsSource + constraints are both absent'). data/index.ts:104 `constraintsSource: { type: 'string' }`. outputSchema has `additionalProperties: true`, so two added report fields pass the walker's shape check. [files: src/analyze/planner/templates/code/index.ts, src/analyze/planner/templates/infra/index.ts, src/analyze/planner/templates/data/index.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The list of sites that read or name constraintsSource, and that build the adherence-report, is complete: the shared check, the three templates, the three family runtimes and one test file.","evidence":"A repo-wide search for `constraintsSource` outside docs/.insrc finds only adherence.ts (214, 349), the three template files, and shared/__tests__/adherence-constraints.test.ts (191, 211); no prompt under src/prompts, no plugin and no doc outside this Story's own artifacts names it. runAdherenceCheck has exactly three callers (code/adherence-check.ts:102, data/adherence-check.ts:110, infra/adherence-check.ts:99); the data runtime builds the report field by field (120-127), so copying the two new fields there is the right site. _resolveConstraintsForTest is used only in adherence-constraints.test.ts (six calls). [files: src/analyze/runtimes/shared/adherence.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/data/adherence-check.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/shared/__tests__/adherence-constraints.test.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/__tests__/scope-sources.test.ts]","action":"Two details the design leaves unsaid, for the build: (1) the seam _resolveConstraintsForTest (adherence.ts:535-545) must also be given or resolve the new repoPath argument, not only return the new shape; (2) scope-sources.test.ts:91 has a second count, `\\brepoPath\\s*=` equals 2, which must go to 1 together with line 90.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The validator has an INV-5 loop with a worded check before the schema's own error, the planner's retry is sent a per-invariant fix hint whose INV-5 text contradicts removing a task, and a root-level anyOf in an inputSchema is safe there.","evidence":"validate.ts:208-232: per task, refusedScopeKind runs first and returns an INV-5 failure, then `paramAjv.compile(tmpl.inputSchema)`; the Ajv is built with `strict: false` (202-207), so `anyOf: [{required:[...]}]` compiles. invariant-fix-hints.ts:85: 'Read the schema error message and fix ONLY the offending property. Do not touch other tasks.' driver.ts:50, 371, 390 render and append the hint. inputSchema is consumed only by validate.ts (ajv) and render-catalog.ts:50-51 (printed as JSON text); it is never handed to a CLI as a structured-output schema, so the cross-vendor refusal of a root union does not apply. [files: src/analyze/planner/validate.ts, src/analyze/planner/invariant-fix-hints.ts, src/analyze/planner/driver.ts, src/analyze/planner/render-catalog.ts]","action":"None. render-catalog.ts is listed as a call site but needs no code change: it prints whatever the schema holds.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The check has one source of its repository (adherenceRepoPath = graphRepoOf of the scope resolved for the template's own family), called twice today, with a source scan that pins the count; a connection scope resolves to the declaring repository.","evidence":"adherence.ts:328-330 `return graphRepoOf(await resolveTaskScope(args.intent.scopeRef, familyOfTemplate(templateId), templateId));`, called at 221 and 394. task-scope.ts:88-90 `return scope.repoPath ?? scope.lookupPath;`. scope.ts:21-23 'the id must be declared by exactly one registered repo, and lookups run in that repo'; 53-55 repoPath is 'the connection's repo'. scope-sources.test.ts:90 asserts the count is 2. Moving the call ahead of resolveConstraints only changes which error comes first for a task that has both a refused scope and no constraints. [files: src/analyze/runtimes/shared/adherence.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/shared/task-scope.ts, src/analyze/context/scope.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/__tests__/scope-sources.test.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A record under the run's directory is shared by a whole plan tree and is safe to read-or-make without a lock: child plans run under the parent's run id, each task is given the run id, and the walk does not run tasks together.","evidence":"walker.ts:326 `const childResult = await executePlan(childNode, intent, runId, opts);` passes the parent's runId; walker.ts:251 hands `task, intent, upstreamOutputs, runId` to execute; a search of walker.ts for `Promise.all` finds nothing, so sibling checks run one after another and the second finds the first's record. paths.ts:100-115 already has analyzeRun(runId) and analyzeTaskOutput under ~/.insrc/analyze/<runId>/, so analyzeConstraintRecord fits the existing layout. [files: src/analyze/executor/walker.ts, src/shared/paths.ts]","action":"None. One thing to weigh in the build: each adherence-report now carries the full constraint list, and the aggregate task renders every upstream output into its prompt, so four checks on one topic repeat the list four times there; Story s3 owns the 'Prompt is too long' aggregator failure, so note it for that Story rather than change this design.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The seams the test strategy relies on exist, and the named tests would fail on today's code.","evidence":"Judging stand-in: dropped-or-failed.test.ts:262-276 uses `runWithRoutingContext(routing, ...)` with `router.resolveProviderForRole`. Enumeration stand-in: RunDocConstraintEnumerateArgs.provider ('a test passes a stand-in'). Scope seam: task-scope.ts:40 _setTaskScopeDepsForTest. Plan walk: walker.ts:80 runExecutor, with result.root.tasksFailed and perTask asserted at dropped-or-failed.test.ts:288-298. Falsifiability: today a task with only a subject passes validatePlan (required is only the subject), today's catalog text names docs.constraint.enumerate and constraintsSource, today no adherence code calls the enumeration and the report has no constraints field, and adherence-constraints.test.ts has exactly two constraintsSource tests (191, 211) to replace. Every acceptance criterion ac1-ac5 has at least one such test. [files: src/analyze/runtimes/__tests__/dropped-or-failed.test.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/shared/task-scope.ts, src/analyze/executor/walker.ts, src/analyze/runtimes/shared/__tests__/adherence-constraints.test.ts]","action":"None. Migration step 4 (the docs update) has no test, which is acceptable for prose.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-10T07:08:09.918Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
